<lesson id="les-l10-04-two-carriers" title="Two carriers to the exchange" level="10" minutes="12" goal="PopCity reaches IXNational through either carrier, so either carrier may die"/>
<step n="1" text="The city buys lines from two national carriers, but only OperatorOne is lit. The line to OperatorTwo is plugged in with both ports turned off: one carrier outage and the city goes dark."/>
<step n="2" text="On PopCity, turn port GigabitEthernet0/1 on. Do the same for GigabitEthernet0/0 on OperatorTwo. OSPF now knows both roads to the exchange."/>
<step n="3" text="Let OperatorOne die in your head: the city must still reach NationalServices through OperatorTwo." check="c1"/>
<step n="4" text="And the other way around: OperatorTwo may die too." check="c2"/>
<step n="5" text="With both carriers up, the city reads the national service as always." check="c3"/>
<check id="c1" kind="outage" from="pc0" to="server0" url="kota:GigabitEthernet0/0" expect="ok" label="CityResident still reaches NationalServices with the OperatorOne line cut"/>
<check id="c2" kind="outage" from="pc0" to="server0" url="kota:GigabitEthernet0/1" expect="ok" label="CityResident still reaches NationalServices with the OperatorTwo line cut"/>
<check id="c3" kind="ping" from="pc0" to="server0" url="" expect="ok" label="CityResident reaches NationalServices"/>
